MapMyVisitors script was loading at `<body>` bottom, rendering outside the footer's dark background area instead of inside it.

## Changes

- **`client/index.html`**: Removed static script tag
- **`client/src/components/Footer.tsx`**: Dynamic script loading via `useEffect`
  - Checks for existing script to prevent duplicates
  - Uses `useRef` to track ownership for cleanup
  - Appends to existing `mapmyvisitors-container` div

## Implementation

```tsx
import { useEffect, useRef } from "react";

export default function Footer() {
  const scriptCreatedRef = useRef(false);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (!document.getElementById('mapmyvisitors')) {
      const script = document.createElement('script');
      script.id = 'mapmyvisitors';
      script.src = 'https://mapmyvisitors.com/map.js?d=...';
      script.async = true;

      const container = document.getElementById('mapmyvisitors-container');
      if (container) {
        container.appendChild(script);
        scriptCreatedRef.current = true;
      }
    }

    return () => {
      if (scriptCreatedRef.current) {
        const scriptElement = document.getElementById('mapmyvisitors');
        scriptElement?.parentNode?.removeChild(scriptElement);
        scriptCreatedRef.current = false;
      }
    };
  }, []);

  return (
    <footer className="bg-gray-900 ...">
      {/* ... */}
      <div id="mapmyvisitors-container" />
    </footer>
  );
}
```

Widget now renders inside footer's dark background area as intended.

