Configures CORS across all 4 microservices with externalized allowed origins and Spring Security integration.

## Changes

- **Properties**: Added `app.cors.allowed-origins` to each service's `application.properties` with env var fallback
- **CorsConfig**: Created `WebMvcConfigurer` implementation in each service injecting origins via `@Value`
- **Security Integration**: Added `.cors(Customizer.withDefaults())` to `SecurityFilterChain` for preflight request handling

## Configuration

```properties
app.cors.allowed-origins=${CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS:http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:3001}
```

```java
@Configuration
public class CorsConfig implements WebMvcConfigurer {
    @Value("${app.cors.allowed-origins}")
    private String[] allowedOrigins;

    @Override
    public void addCorsMappings(CorsRegistry registry) {
        registry.addMapping("/**")
                .allowedOrigins(allowedOrigins)
                .allowedMethods("GET", "POST", "PUT", "DELETE", "OPTIONS")
                .allowedHeaders("Authorization", "Content-Type", "Accept")
                .allowCredentials(true);
    }
}
```

## Security

- Explicit allowed headers instead of wildcards when `allowCredentials(true)`
- No hardcoded origins—configurable per environment

